  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday) \nIssued at 816 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nThe ridge that expands from the Southern Plains up through the\nMidwest on Tuesday will get squished for the lack of a better\ndescription through the week and into the weekend. An incoming upper\nlevel trough will swing through the Central and Northern Plains on \nWednesday, and tries to shove the ridge eastward. The ridge instead \nwill moreso lean eastward onto the an upper level low that is cut off\nand anchored over FL and the Southeast Coast. The cut off low will \nkeep our upper level winds northeasterly and sfc winds mainly \neasterly through Thursday, reducing the true potential of how much we\ncould warm up. Friday, the southwesterly winds aloft ahead of the \ntrough to the north will give a slight push to temps though. \nRegardless, with the strength of the ridge, we will have slightly \nwarmer than normal temps, reaching the mid/upper 60s on Wednesday, \nwith a few of us reaching 70 on Thursday and all of us in the 70s \nFriday and Saturday. Overnight lows will be above freezing through \nthe extended, upper 30s/lower 40s, but still keep cold weather safety\nin mind.",
